  "rendered": "In Table 2[1], the highest reported titer is for the sesquiterpene alcohol ((cid:0) )-α-bisabolol[2] (printed with the minus sign rendered as a (cid) glyph), made by the engineered strain HBQA7 → SMB19[3], which reached 102,300[4] in the table's titer units, i.e. 102,300[5] (mg L^(cid:0) 1)[6]. The conditions listed are a fed-batch[7] cultivation lasting 110[8] h, with the engineering strategy given as Genome integration of the biosynthetic pathway and optimization of[9] precursor supply[10], citing reference [22][11]. The main text describes the same result in more detail: Full chromosomal integration of the pathway enabled an antibiotic-free strain achieving a record 102.3 g L^(cid:0) 1 in a 50-L bioreactor [22].[12] For comparison, the next-highest entries in the table are (E)-nerolidol[13] at 70,500[14] and acetoin[15] at 75,200[16], both also in fed-batch mode.",
